|game_text=Plays on table. While you have 14 or fewer cards in hand, opponent may not remove cards from your hand. Once per turn (even at start of turn), may suspend a [Coruscant] Political Effect for remainder of turn. If Grimtaash just played, may place a card from hand in Used Pile.
|errata_history=This is the errata version PC-E2 of [[Vote Of No Confidence]] (version 3 of 4). The image here is the Players Committee card image of this version. The current text is [[Vote Of No Confidence (Errata 3)]] (PC-E3). Each version below is quoted in full with its dated source. Every published image or slip that differs visibly from the one before is a version, numbered in release order; a printed errata mark that does not match that order is recorded as a PC transcription error (Bill, 12 November 2026).
* '''Original''' ([[Vote Of No Confidence]]): Card image first published 8 July 2018<ref name="v0-1">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/022435b/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Dark/large/voteofnoconfidence.gif voteofnoconfidence.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/022435b 022435b] (8 July 2018, “Set 9 load”).</ref>: “Plays on table. While you have 12 or fewer cards in hand, opponent may not remove cards from your hand (except with Grimtaash). Once per turn (even at start of turn), target a [Coruscant] Political Effect; it is suspended for the remainder of the turn.” Printed: no errata mark; lower-left name “•Little Real Power”. The PC first released this shield with [[Virtual Set 0]] / [[Virtual Set D]] on 24 September 2014. The PC's Holotable image set starts on 8 July 2018, so this is the earliest surviving PC card image; whether the 2014 release slip had the same words is not shown by it.
* '''PC-E1''' ([[Vote Of No Confidence (Errata)]]): Card image published 5 March 2022<ref name="v1-1">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/79618fb/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Dark/large/voteofnoconfidence.gif voteofnoconfidence.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/79618fb 79618fb] (5 March 2022, “Fixing case and making gifs”); high-resolution image <code>ResetDS-Dark/hires/voteofnoconfidence.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/d23ce93 d23ce93] (4 March 2022, “January 2022 Errata images.”).</ref>: “Plays on table. While you have 12 or fewer cards in hand, opponent may not remove cards from your hand (except with Grimtaash). Once per turn (even at start of turn), may target a [Coruscant] Political Effect; it is suspended for the remainder of the turn.” Printed: marked “E1”; lower-left name “Little Real Power”. '''What changed:''' PC errata of January 2022 (the high-resolution image was committed on 4 March 2022 as “January 2022 Errata images.”; image marked “E1”): “target a [Coruscant] Political Effect” becomes “may target a [Coruscant] Political Effect”. The bullet is dropped from the lower-left name, and the image is re-made at a larger size. The PC published a pixel-identical copy of this image on 5 July 2022 (“fixing sizes”; file format change only, no visible change).
* '''PC-E2''' (this page): Card image published 22 July 2024<ref name="v2-1">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/6c22b09/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Dark/large/voteofnoconfidence.gif voteofnoconfidence.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/6c22b09 6c22b09] (22 July 2024, “Fixing case and making gifs”); high-resolution image <code>ResetDS-Dark/hires/voteofnoconfidence.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/a546b30 a546b30] (21 July 2024, “Set 23 Errata”).</ref>: “Plays on table. While you have 14 or fewer cards in hand, opponent may not remove cards from your hand. Once per turn (even at start of turn), may suspend a [Coruscant] Political Effect for remainder of turn. If Grimtaash just played, may place a card from hand in Used Pile.” Printed: marked “E2”; lower-left name “Little Real Power”. '''What changed:''' PC errata released with [[Virtual Set 23]] and the July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit<ref name="dskit2024">Players Committee, [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/DShieldUpdateKit_2024_July.pdf July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit] (PDF, 3 pages, “SWCCG Players Committee, July 2024”; file built 2 August 2024), released with [[Virtual Set 23]] (22 July 2024).</ref> (image marked “E2”): “12 or fewer” becomes “14 or fewer”; “(except with Grimtaash)” is removed; “may target a [Coruscant] Political Effect; it is suspended for the remainder of the turn” becomes “may suspend a [Coruscant] Political Effect for remainder of turn”; new last sentence “If Grimtaash just played, may place a card from hand in Used Pile.”
* '''PC-E3''' ([[Vote Of No Confidence (Errata 3)]]): Partial slip in the July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit<ref name="dskit2024-slip">Players Committee, [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/DShieldUpdateKit_2024_July.pdf July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit] (PDF, 3 pages, footer “SWCCG Players Committee, July 2024”; file created 2 August 2024), page 1: partial slip labelled “•Vote Of No Confidence”. Released with [[Virtual Set 23]] (22 July 2024); the PDF itself is dated by its creation date.</ref>: “Plays on table. While you have 14 or fewer cards in hand, opponent may not remove cards from your hand. Once per turn (even at start of turn), may suspend a [Coruscant] Political Effect for remainder of turn. If Grimtaash just played, may place a card from hand in Used Pile.” '''What changed:''' Same words as the 22 July 2024 card image ([[Vote Of No Confidence (Errata 2)]]). The kit prints the card as a partial slip — the title bar and lore, a blank white area where the picture is, and the game-text box — with the lower-left name and the errata mark “E2” at the bottom, to be laid over a printed card. A separate PC publication that looks visibly different from the card image, so a version (Bill, 11 and 12 November 2026: every publication and every visible change is a version). '''Errata mark:''' the slip prints “E2” but is errata 3 in release order; recorded as printed and listed as a [[Players Committee transcription errors|PC transcription error]] (Bill, 12 November 2026).
